  "SourceScope": "Explicit GPU-related sources and dependency locks only. Concurrent 3D-view changes in the shared worktree are preserved and excluded from this completion claim; shared localization/guide files are fingerprinted in full.",
  "Implemented": [
    "Normal CPU geometry and CUDA use the same rotational sag, verified intersection, normal, Snell refraction and 2D stop-map solver. The initial-structure module adds no optical formulas.",
    "GPU handles implicit aiming, formal rays, TIR with retained incident medium, bulk absorption, physical clipping, diameter-envelope propagation and independent dense validation rays.",
    "Dense validation retains 21 fields, 10x32 integration quadrature, separate boundary/center checks, original wavelengths and hard throughput/target gates. Statistical reductions, material preparation, Adam, manufacturing and control flow remain CPU.",
    "Field-major pupil grids are combined by wavelength. Device buffers and unchanged complete surface data are reused under a runtime lock; no unsafe cross-revision result cache added. CPU fallbacks are never stored as CUDA cache results.",
    "Bounds: 4096 rays x 128 surfaces per GPU trace batch; 101 fields and 100000 rays/wavelength per aiming grid; original derivative graph bounds unchanged. Cancellation checked at batch boundaries.",
    "Exceptional branches retain the CPU extended chief-angle continuation and disclose CpuRecoveryRays; actual GPU aiming/trace and gradient work are stored separately, with resume validation and historical omitted-field compatibility.",
    "Mandatory DLL and exact upstream license payload includes ILGPU.Algorithms, original NCSA and third-party notices; no driver/toolkit or external optical engine redistributed."
  ],
